{"id": "x00175", "text": "- Only the specific element or relationship implicated by a structure-sensitive selector should block a rewrite. Unrelated parts of the document must stay optimizable."}
{"id": "x00176", "text": "**Request (ticket CAT-518):** In the cattrs repo at `/app`, add `partial_structure` to `BaseConverter` and as a top-level function. It returns a `PartialResult` with these fields:"}
{"id": "x00177", "text": "- `validated_to_result` turns an `Invalid` into `Failure(tuple_of_errors)`."}
{"id": "x00178", "text": "- `combine` is implemented as `first.apply(second.map(lambda two: lambda one: function(one, two)))`. This gives left-to-right error order, because `apply` computes `self.errs + container.errs`."}
{"id": "x00179", "text": "- Updated: `returns/converters.py`, `returns/methods/cond.py`, `returns/contrib/hypothesis/containers.py`, `returns/pointfree/__init__.py`."}
{"id": "x00180", "text": "- Preserve existing comments and docstrings unrelated to my changes."}
{"id": "x00181", "text": "- `npx vitest run tests/window.test.ts` passed 3/3. Run it from `/app/drizzle-orm`."}
{"id": "x00182", "text": "- **Job:** `backend/pkg/scheduler/drift_detection_job.go`."}
{"id": "x00183", "text": "4. Optional extras if time allows, not required: run `dprint check` for lint, run `cd drizzle-orm && npx tsc --noEmit -p .` once more, and add `.window()` end-to-end tests per dialect."}
{"id": "x00184", "text": "- The submit command must be issued alone and last."}
{"id": "x00185", "text": "- A plain `git push -u origin feature/partial-structuring-recovery` was **rejected as non-fast-forward**."}
{"id": "x00186", "text": "- Current branch is `feature/structural-selector-preservation`, with one local commit on top of main. The working tree is clean."}
{"id": "x00187", "text": "- Selectors that fail to parse or contain pseudo-elements, nesting or `:scope` are skipped."}
{"id": "x00188", "text": "- `Invalid.lash` receives the whole error tuple."}
{"id": "x00189", "text": "- `partial_structure(converter, obj, cl)` and the internal `_partial` function."}
{"id": "x00190", "text": "- `windowSum` and `windowAvg` map with `String` and are typed `string | null`. `windowCount` and the ranking helpers map with `Number`."}
{"id": "x00191", "text": "- Run `go test ./internal/services -run Drift`."}
{"id": "x00192", "text": "- Working directory `/app`, current branch `feature/partial-structuring-recovery`, clean tree after the 2 commits."}
{"id": "x00193", "text": "- **Offset helpers:** `lag`, `lead`, `firstValue`, `lastValue`, `nthValue`."}
{"id": "x00194", "text": "- Environment IDs: local is \"0\" (`types.LOCAL_DOCKER_ENVIRONMENT_ID`)."}
{"id": "x00195", "text": "- The working tree is clean except for the two local commits. Current branch: `feature/window-function-builders`."}
{"id": "x00196", "text": "- `PartialResult.refine(data)` returns a new `PartialResult`, fixing failed fields with new data while preserving structured fields."}
{"id": "x00197", "text": "- Absent optional TypedDict keys are in neither set."}
{"id": "x00198", "text": "- Doctests passed: `python -m pytest -q -c /dev/null --doctest-modules returns/validated.py returns/converters.py returns/pointfree`, 39 passed."}
{"id": "x00199", "text": "**Current task (ticket RET-292):** In the `returns` repo at `/app` (it replaced drizzle-orm), add an error-accumulating `Validated` container with subtypes `Valid` and `Invalid`."}
